/*!
\mainpage Home

Welcome to the manual of the Virtual Experimentation Framework software suite!

New to the VEF?
---------------
- \ref page_gettingstarted describes the installation of the VEF software.
- \ref guided_tour gives a step-by-step tour of some typical use cases where the VEF is applied.

Ready to run your own VEF simulations?
---------------
The \ref user_reference presents the main components of the VEF and discusses 
  how to operate them. 
  It covers:
- \ref page_conventions that explain how to specify the inputs and interpret the outputs, 
- \ref page_expert_mode that provides a complete control over all the knobs  in the VEF software, 
- \ref page_simple_mode that helps to carry out standard tasks with minimal
effort, while sticking to pre-defined defaults,
- \ref page_utilities that facilitate a more integral use of the VEF, 
- \ref page_theory that introduces the foundations of the VEF software and multi-scale crystal
plasticity models it utilizes.
- \ref page_licensing that discusses how to use the licensing options.

Need a helping hand?
--------------- 

Included \ref page_tutorials are:
  - \ref guided_tour "Guided tour in the expert mode"
  - \ref tutorial_swift "Identification of Swift parameters from tensile data"
  
\ref page_resources contain:
  - \ref examples - a collection of sample problems bundled with the VEF.
  - \ref support

*/


